From 2a6ef3c86ca6265501b9634649ba6faf5ff157fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Gunthorpe <jgg@nvidia.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 19:56:13 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] drtm: Build TCB hash tables for selected algorithm

interface013 and interface014 hard-coded a SHA-256-sized zero digest in
every DRTM_SET_TCB_HASH table entry. Newer firmware rejects the call
because its selected hash algorithm does not match.

DEN0113 1.4B section 3.9.2 requires the caller to compute TCB hashes
"using the hash algorithm in use by the DRTM implementation ... determined
using the DRTM_FEATURES function," and Table 16
(TCB_HASH_TABLE definition) ties the Hash algorithm field and each
entry's digest length to that same algorithm (SHA-256: 32 bytes,
SHA-384: 48 bytes, SHA-512: 64 bytes). Add
val_drtm_init_tcb_hash_table() to size and tag each table entry
from the algorithm reported by DRTM_FEATURES, and use it from both
tests.

Signed-off-by: Jason Gunthorpe <jgg@nvidia.com>
